[6] verdict quantities
    (i)   closed forms: Var(G|0) = beta^2 sin^2(th/2) V0(beta cos(th/2));  E[H|0] = (beta/2)cos(th/2)<A0>(beta cos(th/2))
    (ii)  V0(0) = 0.011059293773 [T, h1e] ;  B^2 V0 -> 1/36 [C->T] ;  <A0>(0)=0.357411353, <A0>(inf)=1/2
    (iii) ratio Var/E[H] = 2 beta sin^2(th/2) V0(B) / (c <A0>(B)) ~ sin^2/(18 c^3 <A0> beta)  -> 0: LARGE beta WINS
    (iv)  theta=pi exactly: Var=beta^2 V0, E[H]=0 for ALL beta -> inequality fails for every beta>0,
          NOT at beta*: beta*=4.306608 is the root of Var(G)=E[H+Phi'']=W0, the beta-free Jacobian term.
    (v)   L=2 (p19, beta in [1,6]): Var(F)/E[kappa] = 0.505, 0.787, 0.848, 0.889 -> 1 from below,
          1 - D/S = 0.483 beta^-0.834, Gpp(0) > 0 throughout (0.2835 -> 0.5913).  No crossing in window.
    (vi)  exponent of Var in p19's own window: single plaquette gives k=1.824 (th=0.9pi) ... k=2.000 (th=pi)

Clay 0%.  No QED.

